From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:45:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] bus: fsl-mc: add compat_ioctl to the uapi device

fsl_mc_uapi_dev_fops has no .compat_ioctl, so FSL_MC_SEND_MC_COMMAND
from a compat task (AArch32 or ILP32) fails with ENOTTY. The command
takes a pointer to struct fsl_mc_command, a u64 header and seven u64
parameters with the same layout for every ABI, so compat_ptr_ioctl() is
enough.

Signed-off-by: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/bus/fsl-mc/fsl-mc-uapi.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bus/fsl-mc/fsl-mc-uapi.c b/drivers/bus/fsl-mc/fsl-mc-uapi.c
index a376ec661653..d94c60d32086 100644
--- a/drivers/bus/fsl-mc/fsl-mc-uapi.c
+++ b/drivers/bus/fsl-mc/fsl-mc-uapi.c
@@ -568,6 +568,7 @@ static const struct file_operations fsl_mc_uapi_dev_fops = {
 	.open = fsl_mc_uapi_dev_open,
 	.release = fsl_mc_uapi_dev_release,
 	.unlocked_ioctl = fsl_mc_uapi_dev_ioctl,
+	.compat_ioctl = compat_ptr_ioctl,
 };
 
 int fsl_mc_uapi_create_device_file(struct fsl_mc_bus *mc_bus)
-- 
2.43.0

